Description: every menu of an application at once, from its header bar
 Buffet Menu gives GTK 3 applications that have a menu bar, such as Xed,
 Nemo, LibreOffice and Inkscape, a header bar with a Buffet button. The
 button opens all of the application's menus at once, laid out side by side
 in rows, in place of the menu bar.
 .
 Choose the applications in Buffet Menu's window. They don't change: their
 menu bar is published with appmenu-gtk-module and shown by Buffet Menu,
 with the items' keyboard shortcuts, ticks and greyed-out states. Each
 application's Buffet menu has its own layout settings.
 .
 It works on X11 desktops such as Cinnamon, MATE and Xfce.
